{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.BraidKnot.KeystoneValueMapSynthesis","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.KeystoneValueMapSynthesis","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.BraidKnot.KeystoneSelfDualSpectralNarrowing","lean:module:QOU.BraidKnot.KeystonePerronFrobeniusGroundState"],"declarations":2,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Keystone.keystone_value_map_unique","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Keystone.keystone_value_map_unique","kind":"theorem","line":65,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/KeystoneValueMapSynthesis.lean#L65-L72","doc":"Corollary of leg (B): the value-map target is the *unique* such vector — two positive,\n`k`-normalised fusion-ground eigenvectors agree (independent of the self-dual transform). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Keystone.keystone_value_map_pinned","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Keystone.keystone_value_map_pinned","kind":"theorem","line":38,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/KeystoneValueMapSynthesis.lean#L38-L63","doc":"**Keystone value-map synthesis (sorry-free): the target is uniquely `d_q`, self-dual, and its\n`S`-eigenvalue is `±1`.**\n\nGiven\n* a self-dual transform `T` (`S² = C`, leg (C)),\n* the Perron–Frobenius selection `[PerronFrobeniusGroundState N rho d]` (leg (B)),\n* the self-duality of the quantum dimensions `C d = d` (leg (A): `d` lies in the `C = +1` sector),\n\nany positive eigenvector `v` of the fusion operator `N` at the Frobenius eigenvalue that is normalised\nto agree with `d` at one index `k` and is simultaneously an `S`-eigenvector with eigenvalue `ζ`\nsatisfies **`v = d` and `ζ² = 1`**.  So the value-map target is pinned to the quantum-dimension vector,\nwhich sits in the self-dual sector where `S` acts by `±1` — the full narrowing, in one line. ","signatureChunk":0}]}